   "chronos-forecasting 2.3.2 instead of the (unpinned) version current when the leaderboard row was produced. From 2.1.0 onwards Chronos-Bolt's long-horizon (H>64) heuristic feeds all nine quantile paths back into the context and takes empirical quantiles of the resulting 81 paths; version <=2.0.0 fed only the median path back (see `central_idx` in chronos/chronos_bolt.py). This is the sole cause of the 22 flagged configs: all are medium/long term, MASE (a median statistic) matches to <3% while WQL improves by 5-10%. Pinning chronos-forecasting<=2.0.0 would reproduce the leaderboard's long-horizon WQL."
